---
// Phase 6 polish: this used to be the Astro starter's guestbook demo, which
// had nothing to do with the planner and left visitors landing on an
// unrelated feature. This is now the app's actual entry point — a short
// intro plus the two real destinations (course browsing, the planner).
import "../styles.css";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en-AU">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>ANU course planner (demo) — COMP4020 prototype</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <nav aria-label="site">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <a href="/courses/">Courses</a>
      <a href="/planner/">Planner</a>
      <a href="/readme/">About</a>
    </nav>
    <main class="home">
      <h1>ANU course planner (demo)</h1>

      <p class="disclaimer" role="note">
        <strong>Prototype, not an official ANU service.</strong> This is a student-built
        course-planning tool for a COMP4020 assignment — it is not Programs and Courses, ANUHub
        or Timetable, and never contacts any real ANU system. Every course, course code and
        session time in this app is fictional demo data for one semester and one demo student.
        There is no login: everyone who opens this app is viewing and editing the same single
        demo student's saved candidates and confirmed enrolment.
      </p>

      <p>
        This prototype helps one demo student pick a semester's worth of courses by seeing how
        their lecture and tutorial times actually fit together on a weekly grid, before locking
        anything in.
      </p>

      <div class="home-actions">
        <a class="primary-action" href="/courses/">
          <span class="primary-action-title">Browse courses</span>
          <span class="primary-action-detail">Search demo courses and build a candidate list</span>
        </a>
        <a class="primary-action" href="/planner/">
          <span class="primary-action-title">Open the planner</span>
          <span class="primary-action-detail">Schedule tutorials, preview the week, confirm a plan</span>
        </a>
      </div>

      <p>
        New to this prototype? Start on the <a href="/courses/">courses page</a> to add a few
        candidates, then switch to the <a href="/planner/">planner</a> to schedule and confirm
        them. See the <a href="/readme/">about page</a> for how the project itself was built.
      </p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
